WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
Bend your arm at the elbow.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.910
Your biceps, at the front of
your upper arm, contracts.

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.190
It pulls your forearm up.

4
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.570
But here's the problem.

5
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.610
A muscle can only pull.

6
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.230
It can never push.

7
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.370
So how do you straighten your
arm again, once it's bent?

8
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.250
In this mission, you'll find
out what your skeleton does

9
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.670
besides holding you up, and
why your bones meet at joints.

10
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.690
Then you'll see how muscles
are arranged around a joint,

11
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.990
like your elbow.

12
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.450
Your mission: explain how you
straighten your arm when a muscle

13
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.140
can only pull.
